in @glass
in @spectral/parent

# Property: every parent_edge in the substrate participates in a
# chain that terminates at the root supervisor without revisiting
# `edge.child`.
#
# SIXTH INSTANCE of bilateral pattern #53 (property/fracture;
# promoted 2026-06-10). First instance: keyword/depth
# (@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth +
# @kintsugi/fracture/keyword; 2026-06-10, 5e68df9 + d908798).
# Second instance: gate/diff-closure
# (@epistemologic/pact/gate_matches_diff_closure +
# @kintsugi/fracture/gate; 2026-06-10, b8755cc + 20c5d97). Third
# instance: symbol/canonical-form
# (@epistemologic/pact/symbol_canonical_form +
# @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift; 2026-06-11, 95f4639 + f083a55).
# Fourth instance: partials/AST-breadth (meta-fracture; 2026-06-11,
# fd344bf + 5c4e3ca). Fifth instance: operator/composition-primitive
# (2026-06-11, 423c7d2 + af670d4). This shard + its sibling fracture
# body (@kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle) are the SIXTH INSTANCE,
# landing at the GRAPH-EDGE altitude: the bilateral pattern applied
# to a SUBSTRATE EDGE rather than a token / literal / symbol
# position.
#
# === The graph-edge altitude (#59 gains a new witness) ===
#
# Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop is altitude-portable; promoted with
# af670d4) named the bilateral signature scaling across declaration
# altitudes (keyword / operator / symbol). This instance landings at
# a NEW altitude: the supervision tree's parent edge — a typed
# substrate edge between two gen_prisms, not a token at any
# declaration site. The bilateral signature absorbs the variant
# cleanly: same `pact + glass + opacity + morphism + splinter(ast)`
# chain, ranging over an edge graph rather than a textual position.
# #59's altitude-portability conjecture gains a witness at the
# graph-structure altitude.
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 (2026-06-10, Mara): every
# gen_prism has exactly one parent. The parent edge is the LIFECYCLE
# edge: the parent owns the child's birth, restart, and death. The
# parent-edge class is ACYCLIC across the substrate. The root
# supervisor self-parents (its parent uuid_spectral byte-equals its
# identity); every non-root gen_prism's parent points strictly
# upward toward the root.
#
# This property names the acyclic invariant as a substrate-altitude
# predicate. The sibling fracture body
# (@kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle) emits the morphism that
# proposes re-parenting to the root when the predicate's
# `failure(opacity_map)` surfaces a cycle.
#
# === Parametric over the substrate's parent_edge set ===
#
# The predicate is parametric over the set of parent_edges in the
# substrate at the moment the property is queried. Each opacity
# surfaces ONE (location, cycle_path) pair where:
#
#   - location names the offending parent_edge's source-of-record
#     (the gen_prism whose parent field forms the cycle; the
#     substrate's located-fact carrier per @glass);
#   - cycle_path is the sequence of uuid_spectral that loops back —
#     the chain of parent traversals from edge.child that revisits
#     edge.child before reaching the root.
#
# Same shape as `keyword_matches_depth` (instance 1) and
# `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth` (instance 4): parametric-
# over-a-set, one opacity per offending site. Same `pact + glass +
# opacity + morphism + splinter(ast)` chain throughout.
#
# === The traversal — substrate-altitude carrier shape ===
#
# Cycle detection requires traversing the parent-edge graph from
# each `edge.child` along the chain `edge.child → edge.parent →
# (edge.parent's parent_edge) → ...` and checking termination at
# the root without revisiting `edge.child`. This IS a fold over
# the parent_edge set keyed by uuid_spectral.
#
# STOP-condition 1 (brief): "if the property requires traversing
# the parent-edge graph at substrate altitude (a fold/recursion)
# and the substrate doesn't have a clean substrate-altitude
# traversal primitive, STOP and surface."
#
# Resolution (NOT a STOP): The substrate's discipline at this
# altitude is to declare the CARRIER SHAPE and leave the body as
# the `\` obligation block. `keyword_matches_depth` does exactly
# this: it declares `declared_keywords(file: ref) -> [text]` as a
# carrier; the realisation layer discharges the traversal (parse
# the file, project the declarations). The cycle detection
# carrier here parallels: declare `parent_edges_in(file: ref) ->
# [parent_edge]` as the carrier of edges to check; declare the
# combined property `parent_acyclic(file: ref) -> transparency`
# as the verdict gate; let the realisation layer discharge the
# fold against the substrate's parent-edge graph.
#
# The substrate already names the @epistemologic/properties as
# the carrier altitude for traversal-based predicates (per
# [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]). The fold
# discipline lives at the realisation layer's
# @code/metalogue/materialize step (per docs/specs/spectral-
# runtime.md §5's ouroboros pipeline); the substrate names the
# rule, the realisation discharges the traversal. NOT a STOP —
# the discipline is exactly to declare the carrier and forward-
# promise the realisation.
#
# === Verdict surface ===
#
# Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
#   success              -- every parent_edge in the substrate
#                          participates in a chain that terminates
#                          at the root supervisor without
#                          revisiting `edge.child`.
#   failure(opacity_map) -- some parent_edge's chain revisits
#                          `edge.child` before reaching the root.
#                          Each opacity names ONE (location,
#                          cycle_path) pair — one offending
#                          gen_prism's parent field plus the
#                          sequence of uuid_spectral that loops
#                          back.
#   partial(opacity_map) -- multiple parent_edges surveyed, some
#                          terminate cleanly and some loop.
#
# Located transparency (not @glass.verdict): the kintsugi loop
# consumes the opacity_map to direct mutation. Each opacity names
# ONE offending parent_edge site; the fracture body
# (@kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle) realises the rule by lifting
# violations through kintsugi — re-parenting the offending child
# to the root supervisor (breaking the cycle by promoting the
# child up the supervision tree). The property names the rule;
# the fracture realises it; the kintsugi loop is the bridge.
#
# === Why re-parent to root (not terminate) ===
#
# STOP-condition 3 (brief): "if 're-parent to root' isn't the
# substrate-pull-correct correction (e.g., the substrate prefers
# to nullify the cycle by terminating the offending gen_prism),
# STOP and surface."
#
# Resolution (NOT a STOP): The substrate's kintsugi discipline is
# variety-PRESERVING (per [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]];
# Ashby's requisite variety lifted to @io). A cycle in the
# parent-edge graph is a structural violation; the
# substrate-pull-correct correction is the MINIMUM-VARIETY-LOSS
# move that restores the invariant.
#
# Two candidate corrections:
#
#   (a) Re-parent to root: the offending child's parent field is
#       set to the root supervisor's uuid_spectral. The gen_prism
#       continues to exist; the supervision tree gains a new
#       direct child of root; the cycle is broken because root's
#       parent self-references (terminates the chain).
#       Variety cost: ONE edge changes (the offending child's
#       parent field).
#
#   (b) Terminate the offending gen_prism: the gen_prism exits via
#       `gen_prism.terminate() -> au` (per
#       shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror); the registry shard
#       advances; the supervision tree LOSES a node and ALL its
#       descendant edges. Variety cost: ONE node + N descendant
#       edges + N descendant nodes.
#
# Correction (a) preserves the substrate's variety; correction
# (b) destroys it. The substrate-pull-correct discipline (per
# [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]]: kintsugi preserves
# variety unless variety LOSS is required to preserve a
# higher-altitude invariant) is (a) — re-parent to root, preserve
# the gen_prism, break the cycle by upward promotion.
#
# The root supervisor self-parents by construction (per
# docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3); attaching the offending
# child to root cannot create a new cycle (root's parent is root
# itself; the chain terminates immediately at the next traversal).
# The correction is structurally guaranteed to break the cycle.
#
# NOT a STOP — the variety-preservation argument is the
# substrate's existing discipline; this property names that
# discipline at the parent-edge altitude.
#
# === Cybernetic ancestor ===
#
# Recognition #37 (`requires` IS a Paskian agreement; promoted
# 2026-06-10) names `pact` as the property-declaration form. pact
# replaces the conversation-era `grammar` keyword as the surface
# for declaring properties; the rule names `pact` directly below.
#
# Engineering ancestor: every supervision tree's parentage
# invariant (BEAM's `:supervisor` discipline, systemd's cgroup
# hierarchy, Kubernetes' owner references) implicitly assumes
# acyclic parentage; the contribution here is *typing* the
# invariant at the substrate altitude so the kintsugi loop reads
# it directly.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   acyclic graph       Cayley (1857) On the theory of the
#                       analytical forms called trees; the
#                       discipline of trees as acyclic connected
#                       graphs. The substrate's reading is Knuth
#                       (1968) The Art of Computer Programming
#                       Vol. 1 §2.3 — the rooted tree's parent
#                       function IS a single-direction edge with
#                       the acyclic invariant.
#   supervision tree    Armstrong (1996) Programming Erlang; the
#                       BEAM supervision tree's let-it-crash
#                       discipline; the supervisor's invariant
#                       fires on each child against the parent
#                       edge. The substrate's reading is the
#                       BEAM application/0 topology lifted to
#                       @spectral via shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror.
#   cycle detection     Tarjan (1972) Depth-first search and
#                       linear graph algorithms; the strongly-
#                       connected components decomposition. The
#                       substrate's reading is the per-edge fold
#                       at the realisation layer: each
#                       parent_edge's chain is traversed; a
#                       revisit signals a cycle.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the parent-edge
# acyclic invariant so the kintsugi loop reads it. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 (the
#               supervision tree's parent-edge invariant; the
#               root supervisor self-parents; every non-root
#               gen_prism's chain terminates at the root).
#               Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop is altitude-
#               portable; promoted 2026-06-11) — this instance
#               witnesses portability to the graph-edge altitude.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (opacity / transparency are substrate
#                      vocabulary; the predicate emits typed
#                      carriers throughout),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (the bilateral pattern this is the sixth
#                      instance of; first instance at the graph-
#                      edge altitude),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]]
#                      (Ashby's requisite variety grounds the
#                      re-parent-to-root correction over
#                      termination; variety-preserving is the
#                      substrate-pull-correct discipline),
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (the
#                      SpectralSupervisor precedent; the
#                      supervision tree this invariant structures),
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the
#                      parent edge is set at start_child; the
#                      registry shard advances by one settle when
#                      a parent edge is established),
#                      [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]] (the
#                      architectural surface: sheaf restriction
#                      maps live at entanglement, NOT parent; the
#                      cellular-sheaf reading is downstream of
#                      substrate at entanglement),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (the substrate's loss carrier IS the
#                      epistemologic property altitude; this
#                      property fits the discipline),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity is the
#                      typed carrier; no bare (location,
#                      cycle_path) tuple escapes).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@kintsugi/oscillate`'s
#                  `active_pass` reads this property's
#                  transparency when composing the per-pulse
#                  candidate morphism_set; the binding lands when
#                  the kintsugi loop substrate-pulls. This shard
#                  does NOT pull `@kintsugi/oscillate` or
#                  `@kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle`; the
#                  substrate-altitude arrow points upward (the
#                  loop and the fracture body consume this
#                  property; not the other way around).
# Related shards: spectral/parent.mirror (the typed edge this
#                 property ranges over; sibling tick),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle.mirror (the
#                 sibling fracture body; the operational half of
#                 this bilateral instance — proposes re-parenting
#                 the offending child to the root supervisor),
#                 spectral/gen_prism.mirror (the gen_prism's
#                 parent field is the per-record carrier this
#                 property checks; commit ae965ca),
#                 spectral/supervisor.mirror (the lifecycle-owner
#                 whose start_child sets the parent edge; commit
#                 452ccb2),
#                 spectral/registry.mirror (the supervisor's
#                 child index; orthogonal to parent — the
#                 registry indexes children, parent edges point
#                 the other way; commit 489211e),
#                 epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (FIRST
#                 INSTANCE, parametric-over-set per declaration),
#                 epistemologic/property/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/partials_align.mirror
#                 (FOURTH INSTANCE, meta-fracture, parametric-
#                 over-computation),
#                 epistemologic/property/operator_matches_composition_primitive.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/operator_match.mirror
#                 (FIFTH INSTANCE, operator altitude, parametric-
#                 over-table),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                 `location`, `transparency`).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/pact/parent_acyclic` as a species
# under the @epistemologic/property family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2 from the
# @epistemologic family root; per recognition #46 it uses `pact`
# (the property-declaration form; recognition #37 promoted
# 2026-06-10).

pact @epistemologic/pact/parent_acyclic {
  # The carrier — the substrate's set of parent_edges at the
  # moment the property is queried. The realisation layer
  # discharges this by projecting `parent_edge` records from
  # every gen_prism in the substrate's supervision tree (the
  # gen_prism.parent field + the gen_prism.identity field form
  # one parent_edge per gen_prism).
  parent_edges_in(file: ref) -> [parent_edge] { \ }

  # The combined property: every parent_edge in the substrate
  # participates in a chain that terminates at the root
  # supervisor without revisiting `edge.child`.
  #
  # The fold (the realisation layer discharges): for each
  # parent_edge in parent_edges_in(file), traverse the chain
  # edge.child → edge.parent → (the parent_edge whose .child ==
  # edge.parent) → ... and check that either:
  #   (a) the chain reaches a self-parenting parent_edge (root
  #       supervisor: edge.child == edge.parent) — termination
  #       at root, OR
  #   (b) the chain revisits the original edge.child before
  #       reaching root — cycle detected.
  #
  # Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
  #   success              -- every parent_edge's chain reaches
  #                          root without revisiting edge.child.
  #   failure(opacity_map) -- some parent_edge's chain revisits
  #                          edge.child; each opacity names ONE
  #                          (location, cycle_path) pair where
  #                          cycle_path is the sequence of
  #                          uuid_spectral that loops back.
  #   partial(opacity_map) -- multiple parent_edges surveyed,
  #                          mixed verdict.
  parent_acyclic(file: ref) -> transparency { \ }
}

out parent_edges_in
out parent_acyclic
out @epistemologic/pact/parent_acyclic
